[thin] Nominal three-millimetre fixture backstop at the strict numerical threshold. The source places the tip datum at Y90.015 and the aft tool face at Y93.015. All eight emitted anchor pairs intersect exactly 3.000000 mm of the actual canonical native solid, with five interior samples per pair. The full unchanged lint reports 3.000 mm at each planar section; these are threshold readings of the authored nominal 3 mm stock, rather than a smaller native wall. Printed dimensions and gauge calibration remain unqualified.
alternatives: Thickening the aft tool wall beyond its nominal 3 mm hides a numerical threshold reading without correcting a smaller native section. Moving the fore face changes the functional tip-setting datum. An actually sub-nominal native wall would require a source correction.
